  "diagnosis": "The 2025\u201103\u201131.basil version removed the top\u2011level `payment_intent` field from the Invoice object and introduced a `payments` array that contains individual payment objects. The original adapter accessed `invoice[\"payment_intent\"]`, causing a KeyError. The repaired function follows the independent audit policy: it validates that `invoice.payments` is a dict and that `payments.data` is a list, then iterates each entry, only extracting IDs from items whose `payment.type` is exactly \"payment_intent\" and whose `payment_intent` pointer is a non\u2011empty string or an object with a non\u2011empty `id`. All other cases return an empty list or skip the item, matching the required contract.",
